# University Rules Assistant — RAG Chatbot

A Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) chatbot that answers student questions using a university rules document.

## Project Overview

This project retrieves relevant university rules and uses a text-generation model to produce answers grounded in the retrieved context. It also displays the source rule and similarity score to help users inspect the response.

## Technologies Used

- Python
- Google Colab
- Sentence Transformers (`all-MiniLM-L6-v2`)
- Scikit-learn
- FLAN-T5 (`google/flan-t5-small`)
- Gradio

## How It Works

1. Load the university rules document.
2. Split the document into text chunks.
3. Convert the chunks into vector embeddings.
4. Retrieve the most relevant chunk using cosine similarity.
5. Generate an answer using the retrieved context.
6. Display the answer, source rule, and similarity score in a Gradio chat interface.

## Features

- Semantic search over university rules
- Context-based answer generation
- Source-rule display
- Similarity score display
- Rejection of questions with insufficient retrieval similarity
- Interactive chatbot interface

## Testing

The chatbot was tested with questions about attendance requirements, student absence rules, identity-card policies, and unsupported hostel-fee information.

## Limitations

- Retrieves only the single best-matching chunk.
- Similarity scores do not guarantee factual accuracy.
- Generated answers may be incomplete or incorrect.
- Intended as a learning prototype, not an official source of university guidance.

## Run the Project

1. Open the notebook included in this repository using Google Colab.
2. Run the setup and model-loading cells.
3. Run the remaining cells in order.
4. Open the Gradio interface and ask questions about the included rules document.

